Z||000000||Alex2004||08-27-2001||05:15 PM||||i noticed it yesterday when i was leaving my friends house the brakes were suddenly mushy, but it wasn't really bad, just different from normal.  Then today i got in my car to move it and while it was idelling i pushed the brake pedal and it went almost to the floor and then the brake light came on, and when i pushed the pedal again it came off, but the pedal is still mushy.  Also i noticed last week the might right rear caliper isn't releasing all the way, it's not pulling the i can notice but whenever i put it in park i can here it like make this rubbing sound or after i get out if i push my car a lil i can hear it.  Do you think there is water or air in my brake lines or what?  What do i need to check?  Thanks<BR>Alex...  <A HREF="mailto:abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com">abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-27-2001||05:19 PM||||check if you have any brake fluid leaking .if not pump up your brake pedal and hold it if it does not come up you probobly need master cyl.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex2004||08-27-2001||05:42 PM||||Well when i pump the pedal w/ the car off the pedal comes up and get hard to push.  But with it running it's acting normal now b/c i moved it a few spots, and i checked the brake fluid, it was fine.  Where do i check for leaks at? LMK<P>Alex...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Primaris||08-28-2001||01:01 AM||||Check for leaks at the wheels.  Inspect the flexable lines and calipers.  These are you most likely spots.<P>------------------<BR>Signatures are a waste of bandwidth!||||reg||1
